comments.body:
Thanks @msteiner-google for the detailed write-up and the repro, made this easy to confirm. Seeing the same on 2.9.2 and on current main: a plain peer ending in COMPLETED never hands control back and the FAILED path gets stuck the same way because the error finish_task has no output.

As a workaround for now try subclassing RemoteA2aAgent to track the final task state in _handle_a2a_response then emitting a finish_task with the artifact text as output (and {"error": ...} on the failure paths). That released the delegation in both cases for me. Could you check whether that works on your end too?

@chelsealong it'd be great to run the same scenarios against #7251 and make sure everything passes before it goes up for review.
